projects.detail_en:
Covering core concepts and recent advances in non-Hermitian physics and open quantum systems:

- Exceptional points (EPs) and spectral singularities: coalescence of eigenvalues and eigenvectors in parameter space;
- Non-Bloch band theory and the generalized Brillouin zone (GBZ): restoration of bulk-boundary correspondence under open boundaries;
- Open quantum systems: derivation, validity, and numerical solution of the Lindblad master equation.

This project focuses on moiré superlattice systems. Starting from square-lattice materials such as black phosphorus, we study band renormalization, flat bands, and correlation effects in twisted bilayers at small twist angles.

Main tasks:
1. Obtain monolayer band structures and Wannier orbitals from DFT (QE, Siesta) to build tight-binding models;
2. Derive and validate the continuum model in the small-angle limit;
3. Analyze the dispersion, topology, and correlation effects of moiré flat bands, exploring new strongly correlated platforms.

The project is currently in the modeling and numerics stage; related study notes are on the blog.
